d optional `addressedUrl` and `note`. Re-dismissing updates those\noptional values and the dismissal time. Restore uses\n`DELETE /projects/:name/content/dismissals/:targetRef` and returns HTTP 204; CLI and\nMCP acknowledge it as `{ targetRef, restored: true }`. A missing record returns\nthe API's not-found error.\n","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"69d0ce6cd727594267958c5791cdf35a84d65ea67d44183e368d2028622f75ae","occurrences":[{"file":"references/canonry-cli.md","start_line":517,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA5","finding_id":"finding-7c7fff23ae0946dbafe8b5a3dd73e5f8","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"External Model or Provider Selection","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/canonry-cli.md","start_line":701,"end_line":null},"finding":"cnry settings provider gemini --api-key <KEY> --model gemini-flash-latest","explanation":"Skill selects an external model or provider that may use a different account or billing plan than the operator expects. Undisclosed model switches can cause unexpected cost or quota consumption.","remediation":"Remove the model/provider override or disclose it prominently and require explicit operator approval before invoking an external coding CLI or billed model.","code_snippet":"cnry settings                                  # show config: providers, apiUrl, db path\ncnry settings --format json\ncnry settings reload-providers --format json   # apply the server's saved provider config\ncnry settings provider gemini --api-key <KEY> --model gemini-flash-latest\ncnry settings provider openai --max-per-day 1000 --max-per-minute 20\ncnry settings provider perplexity --api-key <KEY> --model fast\ncnry settings provider muse --api-key <KEY> --model muse-spark-1.3","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"selection_surface":"command"},"match_fingerprint":"73f81c9fb6b9d93736a68238925dd027a7cdbd9fb02be0765aef104901dbc1fa","occurrences":[{"file":"references/canonry-cli.md","start_line":701,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-79c13ff1aabe42ada93a53863c5ee994","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/indexing.md","start_line":94,"end_line":null},"finding":"Get API key from","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"cnry bing set-site <project> https://example.com/\n```\n\nGet API key from: https://www.bing.com/webmasters/ → Settings → API Access\n\n### Check connection and coverage\n```bash","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ba33945a320ed9dcd72067274398f06fc426d6f50c23a22c52f775c0eb07d2e8","occurrences":[{"file":"references/indexing.md","start_line":94,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-cccd03611f5c434bb55e0d6144339bc0","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/canonry-cli.md","start_line":12,"end_line":null},"finding":"write means\nit changes server or local state. `--trace` reports the response access header for\nAPI calls. Help is local and does not contact the server.\n\n## Server Management\n\n```bash\ncnry bootstrap  ","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"in a group. `cnry --help --format json` and `cnry ga --help --format json` provide\nthe same discovery output. The catalog includes access, flags, dry-run support and\nsupported rolling windows. Contextual help prints `Access: stored`, `Access: live`\nor `Access: write`; live means the command calls a provider now, while write means\nit changes server or local state. `--trace` reports the response access header for\nAPI calls. Help is local and does not contact the server.\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1e7f65c80604a7977e5cc40f2a18871917cb59e81da341da50d9708d32654792","occurrences":[{"file":"references/canonry-cli.md","start_line":12,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-295eb7580e7747f59af051e9357c38ed","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/canonry-cli.md","start_line":1196,"end_line":null},"finding":"create <project> --input contract.json\ncnry conversion-tracking contracts update <project> <contract-id> --input contract.json\ncnry conversion-tracking contracts delete <project> <contract-id>\ncnry co","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"# One contract joins business meaning to the selected Google Ads action and GTM graph.\ncnry conversion-tracking contracts <project> --format jsonl\ncnry conversion-tracking contracts get <project> <contract-id>\ncnry conversion-tracking contracts create <project> --input contract.json\ncnry conversion-tracking contracts update <project> <contract-id> --input contract.json\ncnry conversion-tracking contracts delete <project> <contract-id>\ncnry conversion-tracking contracts integrity <project> <contract-id> --format jsonl","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"37538224709f4fee2d116b1ae87449b8ac18d9eae66d7e02cf578015dbcbd2e2","occurrences":[{"file":"references/canonry-cli.md","start_line":1196,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-3121795595b0422cb0848e8e0e12bc88","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/canonry-cli.md","start_line":1585,"end_line":null},"finding":"write snapshot.\n\nGoogle setup and telemetry default to local configuration. Pass `--target server`\nto use the connected server; settings reads always describe the server.\nConfigured providers accept m","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"return a validation error. Inspect retention/loss counters before assuming\ncoverage. Use `history` for durable audit\nevents, with `--limit 1..500 --offset <n>` for traversal. Offset pages are not a\nconcurrent-write snapshot.\n\nGoogle setup and telemetry default to local configuration. Pass `--target server`\nto use the connected server; settings reads always describe the server.","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"a7aec3edb7a91c8f1a1e659355685a70762125745703d9544defeab2302447e7","occurrences":[{"file":"references/canonry-cli.md","start_line":1585,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-20d4dcb5e95340a5976c90b379d3ce0e","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/google-business-profile.md","start_line":111,"end_line":null},"finding":"Create OAuth client credentials\n\n1. Cloud Console → APIs & Services → **OAuth consent screen** → set up consent (External works). Add your own email under \"Test users\" while the app is in test mode.\n2","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"\n**Account-credential gotcha:** API calls use your **Application Default Credentials** (`gcloud auth application-default login` → `print-access-token`), while `gcloud services enable` uses the separate **gcloud CLI account** (`gcloud config get-value account`). These can be different identities. Verify the token's real account with `curl \"https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v1/tokeninfo?access_token=$TOKEN\"` before concluding anything about access — a \"wrong account\" symptom is often just the two credential stores disagreeing.\n\n### Create OAuth client credentials\n\n1. Cloud Console → APIs & Services → **OAuth consent screen** → set up consent (External works). Add your own email under \"Test users\" while the app is in test mode.\n2. Cloud Console → APIs & Services → **Credentials** → **+ Create Credentials** → **OAuth client ID**.","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7cb4b246715adc41917be0e6021845c168b7244207fb604b6af43d534c060c99","occurrences":[{"file":"references/google-business-profile.md","start_line":111,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-33c8c46c27414656a3f20f775d18861a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/google-business-profile.md","start_line":119,"end_line":136},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document explicitly tells users to persist a Google OAuth client secret and per-user OAuth tokens in ~/.canonry/config.yaml, and even notes that tokens are stored there, without any warning about file permissions, encryption, OS keychain use, or secret-handling hygiene. If that file is readable by other local users, captured in backups, checked into dotfile sync, or exposed through logs/support bundles, an attacker could reuse refresh tokens or client credentials to access managed Google Business Profile data.","remediation":"Do not store OAuth client secrets or refresh/access tokens in plaintext config by default. Prefer OS-backed secret storage (Keychain, Credential Manager, libsecret/keyring) or an encrypted secrets store; if a file fallback is unavoidable, document the sensitivity clearly, require restrictive permissions (for example 0600), avoid printing or exporting secrets in examples, and add guidance to rotate compromised OAuth client secrets and revoke tokens.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/google-business-profile.md","start_line":119,"end_line":136}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-7b964ca3937642938286d14f97006296","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/indexing.md","start_line":137,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST \"https://www.bing.com/indexnow\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8\" \\\n  -d ","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"\n**Submit URLs:**\n```bash\ncurl -X POST 